events:
26日 中共中央同意,钱信忠任卫生部部长、党组书记;
批准钟民任上海市委书记,同意其为市革委会副主任;批准胡景
沄、李飞任中国人民银行党组副书记。

15日 中共中央、国务院发出《关于地市州党政机关机构
改革若干问题的通知》。就机构改革中的具体问题提出如下意
见:(一)积极试行地、市合并;(二)既要管好城市又要管好农
村;(三)保留的地区党政机关应成为名副其实的派出机构;
(四)自治州也要进行机构改革,其机构设置不宜分工过细;
(五)加强领导,保证改革的顺利进行。

11日 中共中央同意,盛树仁任国家经济委员会副主任;
免去王磊的国家经济委员会副主任、党组副书记,李瑞山副主任
职务;免去郭洪涛、宋季文、邱纯甫、史立德、徐驰顾问职务;
陈钝任煤炭工业部副部长;免去刘辉煤炭工业部副部长职务。

3日 中共中央批准,任建新任最高人民法院党组副书记;
同意林祖乙、黄镇东任交通部副部长,免去子刚交通部副部长职
务。

8日 中共中央同意,陈耀邦、刘江任农牧渔业部副部长;
免去朱荣农牧渔业部副部长、党组副书记,萧鹏农牧渔业部副部
长职务。

24日 中共中央批准,郭超人任新华通讯社党组副书记;
庞炳庵任副社长;丁翔起任副社长、党组成员;免去冯健副社
长、党组副书记,杨家祥副社长、党组成员职务。

24日 中共中央同意,郭允中任国家空中交通管制局局
长,任命其为党组书记,免去其中国民用航空局党委书记职务;
任命胡逸洲为中国民用航空局党委书记。

7日 中共中央批准,邓鸿勋任中共江苏省委常委、副书记;
曹鸿鸣任江苏省委副书记;同意刘恕(女)不再担任甘肃省副省长
职务。

13日 中共中央同意,张佑才任财政部副部长;赵宗兼任
人事部党组副书记,人事部副部长;程连昌任人事部党组副书记;
高文不再担任吉林省副省长职务。

25日《党建》杂志第7期刊载中共中央组织部组织局负责
人谈我国党员队伍状况的文章。我党现有4900万党员,从总体上
看,这支队伍是好的。共产党员构成了各条战线英模队伍的主体:
建国40周年前夕,国务院授予全国劳动模范和先进工作者称
号的2790人中,党员占90.6%;
全国总工会授予的5365名“五一”劳动奖章获得者中,党员占
80.5%;
国家科委授予的2219名有突出贡献的中青年专家中,党员占
63.4%;
国家教委表彰的19769名优秀教师(教育工作者、劳动模范)
中,党员占80%;
1990年全国农业劳动模范511人中,党员占83.2%;
全国100名优秀农民企业家中,党员占87%,其中10名最佳
农民企业家都是共产党员;
1979年以来,中央军委和各总部、各军兵种、各大军区授予荣
誉称号的军人中,党员占92.7%,其中中央军委授予荣誉称号的
全部是党员。

同日 中共中央同意,刘锡荣任浙江省纪律检查委员会书记;
免去陈法文的浙江省委常委和省纪律检查委员会书记、常委职务;
免去王钟麓浙江省副省长职务。

23日 中共中央同意,调张丁华任全国总工会党组副书记;
免去于洪恩的全国总工会党组副书记职务,回中国统配煤矿总公
司;免去张丁华的内蒙古自治区党委副书记、常委、委员职务。

translated_text:
On the 19th, the State Council made a decision on institutional reform. The number of directly affiliated institutions of the State Council was adjusted from 19 to 13, and the number of offices was adjusted from 9 to 5. The State Council no longer set up national bureaus under the management of ministries and commissions. The institutions directly under the State Council were adjusted. (--) The State Council set up 13 directly affiliated institutions: National Bureau of Statistics, State Administration of Taxation, State Administration for Industry and Commerce of the People's Republic of China, State Environmental Protection Administration, State Land Administration, Press and Publication Administration of the People's Republic of China (National Copyright Administration), General Administration of Customs of the People's Republic of China, National Tourism Administration of the People's Republic of China, Civil Aviation Administration of China, Legislative Affairs Bureau of the State Council, State Council Religious Affairs Bureau, State Council Counselor's Office, State Council General Office of Institutions, (II) The State Council set up 5 offices: Foreign Affairs Office of the State Council, Overseas Chinese Affairs Office of the State Council, Hong Kong and Macao Affairs Office of the State Council, Special Administrative Region Office of the State Council, Research Office of the State Council, (III) The State Council set up 8 directly affiliated institutions: China Light Industry General Association, China Textile General Association, Xinhua News Agency, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Chinese Academy of Social Sciences, Development Research Center of the State Council, China Meteorological Administration, Patent Office of China, In addition, the State Council also set up the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council and the Information Office of the State Council, The State Council decided to also transfer the following national bureaus to be managed by ministries and commissions
State Technical Supervision Bureau, managed by the State Economic and Trade Commission;
State Building Materials Industry Bureau, managed by the State Economic and Trade Commission;
State Pharmaceutical Administration, managed by the State Economic and Trade Commission;
State Oceanic Administration, managed by the State Science and Technology Commission;
State Seismological Bureau, managed by the State Science and Technology Commission;
State Foreign Experts Bureau, managed by the Ministry of Personnel;
State Language and Writing Commission, managed by the State Education Commission;
State State-owned Assets Administration, managed by the Ministry of Finance;
State Tobacco Monopoly Bureau, managed by the State Economic and Trade Commission;
State Administration of Traditional Chinese Medicine, managed by the Ministry of Health;
State Import and Export Commodity Inspection Bureau, managed by the Ministry of Foreign Trade and Economic Cooperation;
State Cultural Relics Bureau, managed by the Ministry of Culture;
State Administration of Foreign Exchange, managed by the People's Bank of China;
State Grain Reserve Bureau, managed by the Ministry of Domestic Trade;
State Bureau of Surveying and Mapping, managed by the Ministry of Construction.

events:
13日 中共中央同意,宋德福任中央机构编制委员会委员、
办公室主任;免去赵东宛的中央机构编制委员会办公室主任职务;
国林任铁道部副部长;免去石希玉的铁道部副部长职务。

2日 中共中央同意,李贵鲜任中央机构编制委员会副主任;
罗干不再担任中央机构编制委员会副主任职务;胡绳任中央党史
领导小组副组长;免去沙健孙、郑惠中央党史研究室副主任职务。

translated_text:
On the 31st, the General Office of the CPC Central Committee and the General Office of the State Council issued the "Regulations on the Reporting of Personal Major Events by Leading Cadres". The leading cadres referred to in the "Regulations" include: cadres at or above the deputy county (division) level (including deputy county and division level) who hold leadership and non-leadership positions in party organs, people's congress organs, administrative organs, CPPCC organs, judicial organs, and procuratorial organs at all levels. Cadres equivalent to deputy county (division) level and above in social groups and institutions, middle-level and above leading cadres of large and super-large state-owned enterprises, leading cadres of medium-sized state-owned enterprises, leading cadres of large and medium-sized enterprises that implement the corporate system who are appointed by representatives of state-owned shareholders or appointed (including recruitment) by state-owned investment entities, leading cadres elected and approved by the competent authorities, and leading cadres of enterprise party organizations. The Regulations require that the reporter should report the following major events:
(i) The situation of the construction, sale, rental of private houses and participation in collective housing construction by the person, spouse and children living together;
(ii) The handling of weddings, funerals and other celebrations of the person and his/her immediate relatives in which the person has participated (excluding the above-mentioned matters handled only within the immediate family);
(iii) The situation of the person, his/her children marrying foreigners and the situation of the spouse and children going abroad to settle down;
(iv) The situation of the person going abroad for personal reasons and activities abroad;
(v) The situation of the spouse and children being investigated and punished by law enforcement and disciplinary agencies or suspected of crimes;
(vi) The situation of the spouse and children operating individual or private industry and commerce, or contracting or leasing state-owned or collective industrial and commercial enterprises, being employed by foreign-invested enterprises as enterprise supervisors or being employed by foreign enterprises in China, Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan domestic agencies as supervisors.
Other major events that the person believes should be reported to the organization can also be reported.
The Regulations also clarify the acceptance department and handling procedures for leading cadres to report major personal events.
